      "message": "The error message is exactly why I submitted aosp/2809915; would you mind using\n```\nassert_eq!(x, None);\nassert_ne!(x, None);\n```\nin place of `assert!(x.is_{some,none}())` here and below?\n\nThis will automatically (and always) give you an error message like what you want here.\n\nWhen testing a function that `-\u003e Result\u003cOption\u003cT\u003e\u003e`, you could even replace:\n```\nlet x \u003d foo().unwrap();\nassert_eq!(x, None);\n```\nwith\n```\nassert_eq!(foo(), Ok(None));\n```\nto give more context to the panic message than `.unwrap()` holds on its own.",
